### Known cosmetic quirks (not bugs)

- **`transformers.from_pretrained` "meta parameter no-op" warnings on
  v7 model load are benign**. PyTorch 2.4's safetensors loader pre-
  allocates module parameters in "meta" mode then copies real weights
  in via a different code path; the warnings just note that the
  *in-place* copy is a no-op for those meta tensors. Weights are
  actually loaded. Same warnings on Paperspace and laptop.
- **`/opt/venvs/dl-env/`** is the AMI's stock Deep Learning venv;
  not ours. Don't accidentally `source` it -- always use
  `/home/ubuntu/venv`.
- **EasyOCR's first call after a fresh AMI** triggers a ~94 MiB
  model download. Cached at `~/.EasyOCR/model/`; persists across
  reboots.

